;; A text's embedding (seon.vector, docs/vector.md#a-vector-is-its-own-entity), on its own entity
;; pointing at the entity whose text it embeds (:seon.vector/of): a form (its :form/src,
;; content-addressed, so it is embedded once), a wiki section (its :seon.section/text), a task's
;; plan or an eval's record, so what is embedded never appears in that entity's own pull. One stored vector serves every level of the pyramid: a Matryoshka
;; vector's prefix is itself an embedding.
{;; the entity this vector embeds: the vector entity's identity, one per embedded entity, so a vector
 ;; written again (a changed text, another model) replaces it in place (Datahike's upsert on a
 ;; unique identity ref; a [of model] tuple would keep a vector of each model, which nothing reads:
 ;; a vector of another model is due again, docs/vector.md#what-is-embedded)
 :seon.vector/of [:and {:seon.db/identity true :description "The entity this vector embeds (docs/vector.md#a-vector-is-its-own-entity)."} :seon.db/ref]
 ;; the model that made it (its file's sha256): a vector of another model is due again
 :seon.vector/model :string
 ;; the whole vector, f16 (768 dims, 1,536 bytes)
 :seon.vector/f16 bytes?
 ;; the coarse level: the first :seon.config.vector/coarse-dims dims renormalized, as int8, then
 ;; the float scale that maps them back (seon.vector/pack)
 :seon.vector/coarse bytes?
 ;; the transaction of the text it embeds: a text written since makes it due again; indexed, so the
 ;; newest vector written is one seek (seon.context/related-key)
 :seon.vector/text-t [:and {:seon.db/index true} :int]
 ;; the text's whole token count; past :seon.config.vector/max-tokens its first were embedded
 :seon.vector/tokens :int
 :seon.vector/fact [:map {:seon.db/attributes true}
                    [:seon.vector/of :seon.vector/of]
                    [:seon.vector/model :seon.vector/model]
                    [:seon.vector/text-t :seon.vector/text-t]
                    [:seon.vector/tokens :seon.vector/tokens]
                    [:seon.vector/f16 :seon.vector/f16]
                    [:seon.vector/coarse :seon.vector/coarse]]}
